WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:10.000
Four thousand three hundred and fifty dollars. That is what it costs to build an AI system that analyzes the entire Government of Canada.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:22.000
269 investigation pages. 268,488 offshore entities. 7 million government records. Three GPU models running quantum anomaly detection. All self-maintaining.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Phoenix Pay System: 5.2 billion dollars. 1.2 million times more than TENET5. It processes payroll for 290,000 employees. It still doesn't work.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
ArriveCAN: 59.5 million dollars. A COVID questionnaire. 76 percent of subcontractors performed zero documented work. 13,678 times more than TENET5.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Federal AI Strategy: 2.4 billion announced. To do what one veteran with two graphics cards already did. 551,724 times the cost.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
The receipt. Two NVIDIA RTX 5070 Ti: 1,800 dollars. Intel processor: 700. Storage, RAM, power: 1,250. Electricity: 600. Cloud: zero. Licenses: zero. Total: 4,350 dollars.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000
If one disabled veteran can analyze the entire government for 4,350 dollars, what are they spending billions on? The answer is contracts. The procurement system is the product. The spending is the feature.
